  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="17">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIIAtr">VIII Atr</ref> 17</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="17" corresp="#wit-d">And Sunnondaga cypinga forbeode man georne be fullan worldwite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d">And Sunnondaga cypinga forbeode man georne be fullan worldwite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">And Sunday marketings shall be strictly forbidden, under pain of incurring the full civil penalty.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d">And Sunday markets are entirely prohibited, or suffer the full civil penalty.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und Handelsgeschäfte an Sonntagen seien ernstlich bei voller staatlicher Strafe verboten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let Sunday trading be strictly forbidden, on pain of the full secular fine.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 22.1.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">suffer the full civil penalty: Wulfstan does not specify who would suffer in this instance, the market organizer or those participating in it.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
